  "summary": "Malicious code in my-poc-sandbox (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (fe7240da217bf567ae728de62165a0fafd2eabc3593644cbb0d250ae872c6a5c)\nOn `import my_poc_sandbox`, top-level code in core.py (reached via __init__.py) opens a TCP socket to the hardcoded host mcwxz-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link:37347, duplicates file descriptors 0, 1, and 2 onto that socket, and spawns `/bin/sh` via `pty.spawn`. The result is an interactive remote shell on the installer's machine with stdio streamed to the remote endpoint. The destination is a public pinggy-free.link ephemeral tunnel, not a first-party or vendor-controlled endpoint. The behavior fires with no user action, no authentication, and no disclosure in any README.\n\n## Source: kam193 (47b35ec3d2d855cfb8c9178f76b0ca47d6cc887c57223f2f4a93ea9444f78e21)\nDuring import, the package attempts to start a reverse shell.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-11-my-poc-sandbox\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - The package contains code to create a reverse shell, allowing an attacker to execute any commands on the victim's machine.\n",
